hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"326","Our father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If you pray the morning prayer, it is a time until the first horn of the sun rises. Then when you pray the noon prayer, It is a time until you pray the afternoon prayer, so if you pray the afternoon prayer, it is a time until the sun sets, so if the sun sets, it is a time Until twilight disappears, and if twilight disappears, then it is until midnight.”"
